  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are mostly acceptable but weakened on S2 and S3. Northwind secured a 7% sustained-heat failure threshold (above the 5% benchmark) with no automatic sales stop, and a 36-month new-unit shut-off deadline with a 6-year retrofit window and feasibility escape. Halcyon secured customer access to per-model test results, a 36-month fire-suppression deadline, and an 8/100k recall trigger, though that trigger is strict for its Ember 8."
